# Li bootstrap compiler — self-hosted lexer + parser (milestones 1-2 of the Li front end)
# Built by the C++ host:  lic build bootstrap/lic/main.li -o lic-from-li
#
# Subcommands:
#   lic-from-li --version
#   lic-from-li smoke
#   lic-from-li lex <file>       # token dump, same format as C++ `lic lex`
#   lic-from-li parse <file>     # token dump + `parse ok` / `parse error`
#
# The token stream must match the C++ Lexer (compiler/lexer) exactly; the
# parity gate is scripts/check_li_lexer_parity.sh. The parser must accept /
# reject exactly the files the C++ Parser (compiler/parser) does; the gate is
# scripts/check_li_parser_parity.sh, which also diffs the token stream the li
# parser consumes against `lic lex` (token-stream parity vs the C++ parser).
# Token kind codes are the C++ TokenKind enum ordinals:
#   Eof=0 Newline=1 Indent=2 Dedent=3 Ident=4 IntLit=5 FloatLit=6 BinaryLit=7
#   StringLit=8 KwProc=9 KwDef=10 KwType=11 KwAxiom=12 KwTheorem=13 KwLemma=14
#   KwObject=15 KwPrivate=16 KwPublic=17 KwImport=18 KwEnum=19 KwVar=20
#   KwLet=21 KwIf=22 KwElse=23 KwElif=24 KwWhile=25 KwFor=26 KwBreak=27
#   KwContinue=28 KwError=29 KwReturn=30 KwRaises=31 KwExtern=32 KwAsync=33
#   KwAwait=34 KwTrue=35 KwFalse=36 KwAnd=37 KwOr=38 KwNot=39 KwIs=40
#   KwRequires=41 KwEnsures=42 KwProbEnsures=43 KwDecreases=44 KwInvariant=45
#   KwResult=46 KwProtocol=47 KwCallable=48 LParen=49 RParen=50 LBracket=51
#   RBracket=52 LBrace=53 RBrace=54 Comma=55 Colon=56 Arrow=57 Eq=58 Plus=59
#   Minus=60 Star=61 StarStar=62 Slash=63 SlashSlash=64 Percent=65 Le=66 Lt=67
#   Ge=68 Gt=69 EqEq=70 Ne=71 Dot=72 DotDotLt=73 Pipe=74 Ellipsis=75 At=76
#
# Open-VC note: like bootstrap/prover/main.li, the CLI plumbing procs use
# `ensures result == 0 or result == 1` which the native engine leaves open;
# scripts/bootstrap_lic.sh therefore builds with --allow-open-vc (documented).
# The lexer is gated by token-stream parity and the parser by accept/reject
# parity, not by VC discharge.

